**English Prompt:**

> Design a C# application that scans all Excel files in a specified folder and searches their VBA macro code for a specific text string.
>
> **Requirements:**
>
> * The user should provide:
>
>   * The folder path containing the Excel files.
>   * The search string (text to look for).
> * The program should iterate through every Excel file in the folder (including `.xlsm`, `.xls`, and `.xlsb` if supported).
> * For each Excel file:
>
>   * Open the workbook.
>   * Access the VBA Project (Developer → Visual Basic code/modules).
>   * Read all VBA components, including standard modules, class modules, worksheet modules, `ThisWorkbook`, and user forms.
>   * Search the entire VBA code for the specified string (case-insensitive option preferred).
> * If the string is found anywhere in the VBA code:
>
>   * Record the Excel file name.
>   * Optionally record the VBA module name and the line number where the match was found.
> * Continue scanning all Excel files without stopping if one file causes an error.
> * Display the final results in a clear format, showing all matching Excel files.
> * Also save the results to a text file (e.g., `SearchResults.txt`) containing:
>
>   * Excel file name
>   * Full file path
>   * VBA module name (optional)
>   * Line number (optional)
>   * Matching text (optional)
> * If no matches are found, display a message stating that no matching VBA code was found.
>
> **Technical Requirements:**
>
> * Use C# (.NET).
> * Use Microsoft Office Interop Excel (or another suitable library capable of reading VBA projects).
> * Ensure all COM objects are properly released to prevent orphaned Excel processes.
> * Include proper exception handling and logging.
> * The code should be clean, modular, well-commented, and production-ready.
>
> **Note:** The solution should handle password-unprotected VBA projects. If a VBA project is password-protected, skip it gracefully and log the file name as "Protected VBA Project."
